<section class="era">
<div class="era__head"><h2 class="era__title">Building in Tech</h2><span class="era__years">2021–2025</span></div>
<div class="era__body">
<div class="chap"><div class="chap__title">HeyMax.ai <span class="chap__at">— building for customers</span></div>
<div class="prose"><p>B joined <a href="https://heymax.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HeyMax</a> as its first dedicated data hire alongside the founder. Two more data interns joined later.</p><p>Startup life meant wearing a lot of hats: setting up Airflow, working on the data pipelines and models behind the product, building out product analytics in Mixpanel, and handling whatever else needed doing. Build, ship, find the next problem, repeat.</p></div>
<a class="archive-card" href="https://heymax.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
<div class="archive-card__chrome"><span class="archive-card__dot"></span><span class="archive-card__url">heymax.ai</span></div>
<div class="archive-card__shot"><img src="https://media.awhitepen.com/portfolio/tech/heymax-homepage.webp" alt="HeyMax.ai homepage" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
</a>
<div class="refs" data-refs="heymax"></div>
</div>
<div class="chap"><div class="chap__title">Twitter &amp; Standard Chartered <span class="chap__at">— building for businesses</span></div>
<div class="prose">
<p>B's first stint in big corporate came after a decade in television: user and product research, first at Twitter, then at Standard Chartered.</p>
<p>She quickly learnt that doing analytics in a large organisation isn't just about knowing what to do with data. First, you have to find it. Who owns it? Where does it live? Who can give you access? And who knows the unofficial route when the official one leads nowhere?</p>
<p>The work taught her as much about stakeholder management as analysis — talking to people across teams, building relationships, navigating large organisations, and eventually getting the data and context needed to answer the question.</p>
</div><div class="refs" data-refs="corporate"></div></div>
<div class="chap"><div class="chap__title">Mediacorp <span class="chap__at">— Android developer</span></div>
<div class="prose"><p>B's secondment from the newsroom into the technology team working on the platforms that distributed the shows she had spent years producing.</p><p>She worked across the software development lifecycle — requirements, development, testing, CI/CD, deployment and maintenance — alongside a distributed engineering team across time zones. It was a very different view of how television got from the people making it to the people watching it.</p></div>
<div class="cardgrid">
<a class="pcard" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.channelnewsasia" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="pcard__media pcard__media--logo"><img src="https://play-lh.googleusercontent.com/cn-KCFmE5-42HEcK4ucOfshudANtEd9irhmQ4r3kYNB97aUI2nK_Nl3RPw3km26VhJ8_FddOzt__N8X9_6FjSw=s240" alt="CNA app icon" loading="lazy"></span><span class="pcard__body"><span class="pcard__title">CNA</span><span class="pcard__desc">Channel NewsAsia's Android news app.</span><span class="pcard__foot"><span class="pcard__link">play.google.com →</span></span></span></a>
